WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.900
A masked dance.

2
00:00:01.950 --> 00:00:03.320
Two strangers.

3
00:00:03.370 --> 00:00:04.970
Their hands touch.

4
00:00:05.020 --> 00:00:09.450
He begins, "If I profane
with my unworthiest hand".

5
00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:11.010
She answers back.

6
00:00:11.060 --> 00:00:15.570
Line by line, 14 lines of
light stack up beside them,

7
00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:16.830
and they kiss.

8
00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:20.060
Then the light starts
to flicker, like a fuse.

9
00:00:20.110 --> 00:00:25.130
"These violent delights have violent
ends" So is this a love we should admire,

10
00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:27.500
or one we should fear?

11
00:00:27.550 --> 00:00:31.020
In this mission, you'll sort the
many kinds of love in the play,

12
00:00:31.070 --> 00:00:33.090
from courtly to bawdy.

13
00:00:33.140 --> 00:00:37.070
You'll find out why the lovers'
first words make a sonnet they share.

14
00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:41.610
And you'll collect the play's warnings
about love that moves too fast.

15
00:00:41.660 --> 00:00:45.890
Your mission: decide whether this
is the greatest love story ever,

16
00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:47.020
or a warning.
